# gen_kconfig.py deny list for tcp_bbr3.
#
# Force-undef these macros even when the compile probe PASSES. Rationale:
# the probe builds against the ddk GKI tree, whose Module.symvers contains
# these symbols - but the *device* kernel trims exports to its KMI list, so
# modules referencing them fail at insmod with "Unknown symbol" (err -2).
#
# One macro name per line; lines starting with '#' are comments.
#
# Evidence (Xiaomi 14 stock kernel 6.1.138-android14-11, dmesg):
#   tcp_bbr3: Unknown symbol __tcp_send_ack (err -2)
# Without it bbr_compat.h degrades gracefully to flagging ACK_NOW/CWR
# (DCTCP-style immediate-ACK on ECN state change only - cosmetic).

HAVE___TCP_SEND_ACK
